==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{m|es|de||from}} + Old Spanish {{m|osp|onde||whence, from where}}, from {{der|es|la|unde}}.

Replaced Old Spanish {{m|osp|o||where}}, from Latin {{m|la|ubi}}, although the latter survives, in a marginal way, in the form {{m|es|do}}, which is also prefixed with {{m|es|de}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr|+<audio:es-donde.ogg><hmp:dónde>}}

===Adverb===
{{es-adv}}

# {{lb|es|in indirect questions}} [[where]], in [[what]] [[place]]
#: {{ux|es|Deja los libros '''donde''' quieras.|translation=Leave the books '''where''' you want.}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|es|conjunction}}

# {{lb|es|Chile|colloquial}} [[because]]
# {{lb|es|Latin America|colloquial}} [[if]]

===Preposition===
{{head|es|preposition}}

# [[by]], [[near]] to
#: {{ux|es|Estamos '''donde''' la plaza mayor.|We're '''around''' by the main square.}}
# [[round]] {{gloss|at the house of}}
#: {{ux|es|Cenamos '''donde''' Daniel.|We're having dinner ('''round''') at Daniel's place.}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|es|pronoun}}

# {{lb|es|relative}} [[where]], in [[what]] [[place]]
#: {{ux|es|El lugar '''donde''' estamos es secreto.|translation=The place '''where''' we are is secret.}}

